# HTTP response headers for the Cloudflare Pages deployment -- issue #1121.
#
# robots.txt already asks crawlers not to crawl, but Disallow is advisory and
# does not stop Google indexing a URL it learns about elsewhere -- and a
# disallowed page is never fetched, so the meta noindex inside index.html is
# never read either. X-Robots-Tag is the enforcing half of that pair: it rides
# on the response, so a permalink someone pastes into a public channel still
# stays out of the index. The two must agree; securityHeaders.test.ts asserts
# they do.
#
# Cloudflare parses this file and applies it to STATIC ASSET responses only.
# Pages Functions -- /api/* and the /__/auth/* helper proxy -- are untouched,
# which is what keeps that proxy byte-transparent (functions/__/auth/[[path]].ts)
# and is why X-Frame-Options can be DENY: the one same-origin iframe the app
# loads is Firebase's auth helper, served by the Function, not from here.
#
# Deliberately absent:
#   Content-Security-Policy    -- has to be built against the live Firebase,
#                                 Cloud Run and Gemini origins and tested there;
#                                 a guessed policy breaks sign-in silently.
#   Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy -- `same-origin` breaks signInWithPopup, which is
#                                 how Google sign-in works here (AuthProvider).

/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()
